data.content:
Here are the two files:

**Key design points:**

- **Generic** (`@typeparam TItem`) — works with any item type.
- **Code-behind** with `partial class`.
- **Never mutates the input** — copies `Items` into `_items` in `OnParametersSet`.
- **Move Up/Down buttons** are disabled at boundaries.
- After each swap, invokes `OnOrderChanged` with a read-only copy of the reordered list.
- Uses `@key` for efficient diffing.

**Usage** (matching your example):

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private List<TaskItem> tasks = new() { ... };

    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> updated)
    {
        tasks = updated.ToList();
    }
}
```
